# TypeScript

- Do not use `any`. Narrow `unknown` at the boundary (JSON.parse, Redis payloads).
- Domain types live in `src/types`. UI props are dedicated interfaces.
- Repositories return domain objects, never cache envelope types.
- Exhaustive unions: `const _exhaustive: never = value` in the default branch.

```ts
// ❌ BAD
function save(listing: any) { localStorage.setItem('l', listing) }

// ✅ GOOD
function toListing(value: unknown): Listing {
  if (!isListing(value)) throw new TypeError('Invalid listing record');
  return value;
}
```
